catalog_digest.py --diff  run-par-k2-star24full-b6/out/pruned  <this run>/out/pruned
  IDENTICAL — 118 blocks, digest 0b6cb12bb7f5f797

So the shipped 74 now has a certificate that contains NO cap: the search ran to completion with the
noncounting budget effectively infinite, so nothing was truncated anywhere and the enumeration is
exhaustive as a matter of fact, not of fixpoint ritual.

⚑ The 1.36x is itself evidence for the blind spot found this morning. The b6 run reported "budget
never engaged" under the OLD instrumentation (in-loop counter 0), yet removing the cap adds 36% wall.
The cap WAS cutting substantial work at k=2 — through the k-saturated path the in-loop counter could
not see. At k=2 those cuts cost nothing; at k=3 the same mechanism at budget 7 cost 4 tilings
(158 vs 162). Same blindness, different outcome, which is the whole argument against trusting it.
